# SAMPLE — OVERLAY layer (ADR-0036), deliberately EMPTY.
#
# An existing empty directory is a CLAIM: "this deployment declares no domain graphs."
# That is a different statement from an UNSET overlay variable, which means "nobody told me
# where to look" and leaves the composed set unknowable.
#
# The distinction is load-bearing rather than pedantic: a gate that cannot tell those apart
# either refuses a species it was never shown (the 18-row outage) or trusts a set it cannot
# see. So the directory exists, empty, and GRAPH_OVERLAY_DIRS points at it — which also means
# `compose(GRAPH_POLICY_DIR, GRAPH_OVERLAY_DIRS)` executes its overlay branch for the first
# time since it was written, even when there is nothing to overlay.
